charon.plugins.esp-ping.spis =
	Comma separated list of SPIs (hex or decimal) to listen for encrypted
	ESP-ping requests on.

	If empty (the default), the plugin listens for ESP_ECHO_REQUESTs on
	every SA flagged XFRM_SA_XFLAG_ESP_PING (ENCRYPTED_PING_SUPPORTED),
	regardless of peer. Set this to restrict listening to specific SAs,
	e.g. for a monitor scoped to one peer.

charon.plugins.esp-ping.respond = yes
	Whether to reply to requests (responder) or only observe them
	(passive monitor).

	When enabled, the plugin opens a second, send-only socket and replies
	to each request with ESP_ECHO_RESPONSE, on the same SA the request
	arrived on unless the request's R flag names a different return_spi.
	When disabled, the plugin only listens and logs, useful for
	diagnostics without answering on behalf of the responder.
